# RBAC rules

## Existing roles (schema)

- ADMIN
- DOCTOR
- PATIENT
- PHARMACIST
- SUPPORT
- VIEWER

Do not invent new roles without explicit approval.

## Principles

- Backend authorization is the **security boundary**.
- Frontend visibility is **not** security.
- Preserve existing permissions.
- Do not grant permissions simply to make implementation easier.
- New permissions must have a clear business reason.
- Respect patient ownership boundaries (own-record / own-order checks).
- Preserve existing authentication and session/JWT behavior.
- Check both role and resource ownership where applicable.

SUPPORT and VIEWER exist in the role enum; do not assume every route authorizes them—inspect route `authorize(...)` lists before relying on them.
